.TH SHMGET 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
shmget \- obtain a System V shared memory segment
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/shm.h>
.B int shmget(key_t key, size_t size, int flags);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Obtains or creates a Linux System V shared memory segment. IPC_PRIVATE creates
a new segment; IPC_CREAT, IPC_EXCL and permission bits control keyed creation.
Segments persist until marked for removal with shmctl.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns a segment identifier, or \-1 with errno set.
Success leaves errno unchanged.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR shmat (3crunch),
.BR shmctl (3crunch),
.BR shmget (2)
